## Purpose / Description

I use this workflow to enrich a lead list by finding the most relevant decision maker for each company or restaurant based on the company website, target job title, and location context. The goal is to take incomplete rows from a Google Sheet and automatically research who the likely owner, co-owner, founder, executive, or similar key contact is, then write the discovered first name, last name, job title, and researched company name back into the sheet.

The workflow starts from a manual trigger, reads lead records from Google Sheets, filters the rows that still need contact details, and processes them one at a time to keep the research controlled. For each lead, I first retrieve the website title to help identify the real company name behind the domain. Then I use Apify’s Google Search scraping to gather search results about the company and the requested decision maker. If the AI search summary is available, I use that directly; otherwise, I fall back to organic search snippets.

To make the research easier for the AI to reason over, I store the gathered search content in an in-memory vector store using OpenAI embeddings. An OpenAI-powered AI Agent then searches that temporary knowledge base, extracts the best available person, validates that the result looks like a real individual rather than a company name, and formats the answer into a structured JSON-style output. If a perfect match for the requested title is not available, the workflow is designed to look for a nearby senior role or another executive contact, while avoiding weak or irrelevant company-name matches.

Once a usable contact is found, the workflow updates the original Google Sheet row with the researched first name, last name, job title, and company name. It also includes wait steps and error-handling paths so the workflow can continue processing rows even when an API call, AI response, or sheet update temporarily fails.

The critical tools used are Google Sheets for the lead source and destination, a website title extraction request, Apify Google Search Scraper for web research, OpenAI embeddings with an in-memory vector store for contextual retrieval, an OpenAI AI Agent for reasoning and extraction, structured output parsing for clean results, and wait nodes for pacing.

This workflow can be adapted to many similar enrichment tasks. For example, I could use the same pattern to find marketing directors, venue managers, franchise owners, HR leaders, partnership contacts, or any other target role from a list of company domains. To adapt it, I would mainly change the input columns, the target role prompt, the search wording, and the fields written back to the sheet, while keeping the same overall research, retrieval, extraction, and update structure.